# Rule 01. Block is the only root, Box is never a wrapper

Language-agnostic. Applies to any stack and any component syntax.

## Variables

- `{appdir}` is the source root of the app; the shared kit lives in `packages/ui/src`. It depends on the stack:
  `src` for Vite-style projects, `web` for Go projects, and so on.
- Primitives live in `packages/ui/src/ui`.
- Utilities and tag groups live in `packages/ui/src/utils`.

## Goal

The DOM tree must follow HTML5 semantics strictly. Landmarks come only from
`Block`. Nested structure comes only from layout primitives.

## Rules

1. Every component file opens on `Block`. This is critical and has no
   exceptions. A file never starts with `Box`, `Stack`, `Group`, `Grid`, `Card`
   or anything else.
2. One file has exactly one `Block`.
3. `Block` is never nested inside another element of the same file.
   If a nested region needs its own `Block`, move it into a new file and
   import that component. Composition across files is allowed. Nesting
   inside one file is not.
4. `Box` is never a wrapper and never a file root. It appears only inside a
   `Block`, and only where no specialised primitive fits: `Card`, `Stack`,
   `Group`, `Grid`, `List`, `Nav`, `Dialog` and the others found in the kit.
5. `Box` is always a plain nested `div`. It is never a landmark and never
   imitates another primitive.
6. Before using `Box`, search `packages/ui/src/ui` for a primitive that expresses
   the intent. Only if none exists, use `Box`. If the primitive is missing
   and the intent is repeatable, add it to the kit instead of piling up
   `Box`.

## Roots by surface

| Surface | Root |
| --- | --- |
| Application frame | `Block` without `tag`, a viewport container, not a landmark |
| Route or view | `Block` with `tag=section` |
| Page header | `Block` with `tag=header` |
| Primary content | `Block` with `tag=main` and `id=main-content` |
| Complementary column | `Block` with `tag=aside` |

- `header` and `main` are siblings inside the application frame.
- There is exactly one `main` per page.
- The application frame never takes `tag=main`, `section` or `header`.

## Where to look for tags

1. Find the needed element in `packages/ui/src/ui`.
2. If it is not there, check the tag groups in `packages/ui/src/utils`.
3. If it is still missing, extend the kit. Do not write a raw tag in the screen.

## Nested replacements

- Nested navigation or search is `Nav` or `List`, never a nested `Block`.
- A centered modal is `Dialog`, never `Block` plus a dialog role.
- A grid is `Grid`, never `Box` with grid classes.

## Validation

A validator must fail when:

- the first element of a file is not `Block`;
- a file contains more than one `Block`;
- `Block` is found inside another element of the same file;
- `Box` is a file root or a direct wrapper around the whole content;
- the application frame has a landmark `tag`;
- a page has no `main` or has more than one.
